The VP9 Request parser and H.264/HEVC slice controls adapt code by
Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz> from Omacom libva-v4l2_request, commit
4f60c51f7841dd74bb61c94a4ad31e630bbdab01 (GPL-3.0-or-later):
https://github.com/omacom/libva-v4l2_request
Adaptations use the libva-v4l2 queue, storage and reference validation
interfaces. Original copyright and license notices are retained.

libva-v4l2 incorporates source from vaapi-v4l2-bridge by liyifan and
contributors. The original MIT notice is retained in src/api/driver.c.

The bytestream normalizers, VP9 packet construction and private GPU copy
worker adapt work from
Radxa libva-v4l2, commit 6d03c3f8fb19b86f84b2b6c60ff20d1402f0ac41:
https://github.com/radxa-pkg/libva-v4l2

The AV1 OBU normalizer adapts Radxa src/av1.cpp at commit
deee2557dc3ccd00e174ca1249831c008a6d092f, using the shared packet and
queue interfaces. Its MIT notice is retained.

